message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Nepal Ice-Rock Collapse: Climate Screening"
authors:
  - family-names: "Jariwala"
    given-names: "Shreya"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-17"
url: "https://github.com/ShreyaJari/nepal-climate-attribution"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ShreyaJari/nepal-climate-attribution"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - geoai
  - remote-sensing
  - earth-observation
  - climate-screening
  - era5-land
  - anomaly-detection
abstract: >
  A two-method screening analysis of thermal conditions before the August
  2026 Langtang Lirung ice-rock collapse, combining trend-based statistics
  and a VAE-based anomaly detector on ERA5-Land reanalysis to test whether
  pre-event warmth was unusual against a 76-year baseline. Not a formal
  climate attribution study; explicitly scoped as screening.
